    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence supports holding AAPL at current levels rather than forcing a directional call. The medium-term trend is genuinely intact \u2014 price sits 11.1% above a rising 50-SMA and 13.7% above a rising 200-SMA, with excellent fundamentals ($62.6B operating cash flow, $61B returned to shareholders) that preclude a Sell. However, the immediate tape argues against adding: the June 21 session closed down on record volume (241.8M shares, 3.3x average), RSI collapsed from 79.58 to 61.68, MACD histogram decayed 75%, and the stock failed to hold above $208 after the $214.62 high. The stock is extended 11% above its 50-SMA after a 22% run, leaving a mean-reversion gap to $184.95. Per the plan, do not chase at $205; instead wait for a pullback into the $198-200 support zone (improving risk-reward to ~1:3) or a confirmed reclaim of $214.62 on strong volume. Trim on a decisive close below the Bollinger middle band at $198.33; the structural invalidation point is the 50-SMA at $184.95.\n\n**Entry Price**: 199.0\n\n**Stop Loss**: 195.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current position; no new exposure at $205. Any incremental add should be modest (partial add only) given elevated volatility (ATR $4.76, realized vol 33.3%).\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
